  "takeaways": [
    "NtQueryVirtualMemory has a WDK-documented basic class; its larger PHNT selector family has separate contracts.",
    "A process-protection query, process debugger state and handle metadata describe different observations.",
    "Process instrumentation callbacks concern kernel-to-user transitions, not kernel ownership of an entire syscall.",
    "The BattlEye examples are historical researcher reconstructions, not evidence of a current bypass."
